      "claim": "Aliskiren, a hydroxyethylene peptidomimetic with high molecular weight and multiple H-bond donors/acceptors, has human oral bioavailability of only 2.6–5%; L2 adds that intestinal P-gp contributes to its low oral bioavailability in rat, while the qualitative statement that it is 'sufficient for oral use' does not imply F ≥ 20%.",
