      "claim": "Octreotide and GHRP-6 show very low human oral bioavailability (~0.3–0.6% and ~0.3%); L2 rat values of ~1% for GHRP-6 reinforce low F, whereas mouse relative-to-subcutaneous values for octreotide are not absolute oral F and do not change the assessment.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C18","C27","C29","C10","C20","C26","C30","C37","C31","C32"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Additional low-F references all fall below 20%: revefenacin <3%, alvimopan 6% (with L2 surgical 1.9-fold increase still ~11% and poor canine absorption), tilidine 3–7.6%, cromolyn ~1%, and selegiline 10%.",
      "card_ids": ["C04","C13","C15","C39","C06","C07","C16","C22","C33","C35","C03","C08","C25","C34","C11","C24","C28","C38","C40","C14"]
    },
